From e1ff5de7fa47ad43044d935438d69c24fcbfa2bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:40:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] rdna-boosts: block 07: k-quant boosts (mmvq VDR, Q6_K
 MMQ, Q1_0, grid pad)

- old-10: per-type mmvq VDR/nwarps for Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0, dense Q6_K VDR=2
  and the MoE-expert VDR split.
- old-04 MMQ: GGML_CUDA_MMQ_J_MAX and the mmq-vec-dot x_scale/x_df hoist.
- old-15: the Q1_0 ggml_cuda_byte_perm port (vecdotq.cuh + mmq-load-tiles.cuh),
  the gfx1201 grid-stall pad (common.cuh + mmvf.cu), the mmvf multi-token
  cross-warp reduction and the mmq-vec-dot #pragma unroll 1 for gfx12.
- old-04's MUL_MAT Q6_K/Q8_0 test shapes.
- r169: dense Q6_K keeps upstream #30517's VDR=2 on every arch (measured on
  gfx1151: within noise of VDR=1 at B=1/B=4 and d16384, +1.2 % at batched B=8,
  width-pure against draft-mtp).  -DGGML_HIP_Q6K_DENSE_VDR1 restores the
  pre-#30517 VDR=1 association order for a consumer that gates on output
  identity; the MoE-expert VDR is per kernel and unaffected.

NOTE: the mmvq multi-row/row-loop decode hunks (old-15 PR #57) are NOT here --
they are interleaved with the fused-MoE item-split in the same function and are
deferred to 09 (see PHASE1-STATUS.md).

Re-based onto a691b2345 (mmvq.cu conflicted, 2 hunks: the per-architecture MMVQ table
id).  The block splits the old combined mapping -- RDNA3_5 (gfx1151) gets its own table
(nwarps swept), real RDNA2 (gfx103x) gets the Navi21 table -- where upstream maps all of
RDNA2 || RDNA3_5 to the RDNA2 table.  The delivery's split is kept and upstream's new
RDNA4_M family is folded into it (RDNA4_M -> the RDNA2 table) on both the device and the
host table-id paths.  Build green; same-seed greedy text byte-identical with MMVQ on/off
(33 chars, sha 3de206c8878b) on Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B.
